; `load-wav` bound to a LOCAL rather than assigned to a dynamic global:
; the call is an ordinary value-position `[f32]` producer (the VM's
; `HostOp::LoadWav` writes a fresh heap cell, and whole-global
; assignment goes through the generic `RegionFromHeap` path — there is
; no global-assignment fast path for a value-position call to fall
; outside of). The tree-walker binds a plain `Value::Array`.
@cpu
(defn main []
  (let [samples (load-wav "data/audio/test_sample.wav")]
    (print (array-length samples))))
